/* Adapted from analysis_prospective.sas (hajinjang-epi/screentime_isotemporal_substitution)
   The %iso_inc macro is the paper's core isotemporal-substitution model: a logistic
   regression of obesity incidence on daily time-use covariates (sleep, outdoor time,
   study time, etc.) plus one screen-time component, so that swapping one covariate's
   coefficient for another represents reallocating a fixed number of minutes between
   activities. Model structure, class statement, and macro body are unmodified from
   the source file; only the input data below is synthetic (mock time-use panel rows
   in place of the KCYPS2018 survey extract the original script reads via a local
   OneDrive libname). */

